Validation Reference

Validation Objective

Demonstrate that the operating-context interpretation capability enables the Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture (AVIA) to establish meaningful and sufficiently reliable contextual understanding for adaptive decision-making.

---

Validation Method

Validation shall be performed through one or more of the following methods:

Method| Purpose
Operational Evaluation| Assess contextual interpretation under representative operating conditions.
Scenario-Based Assessment| Evaluate interpretation across changing, ambiguous, and interacting operating conditions.
Stakeholder Acceptance| Confirm that the interpreted context provides the level of understanding required by approved downstream functions.

---

Validation Reference

Detailed validation scenarios, operational evaluations, acceptance criteria, and supporting evidence shall be maintained within the AVIA Validation domain and referenced from this objective.

---

Validation Success Criteria

Validation shall demonstrate that the system:

- Establishes an operational context that meaningfully represents relevant observed conditions.
- Maintains contextual understanding as operating conditions change.
- Provides sufficient contextual information to support downstream adaptive decision-making.
- Appropriately represents uncertainty where contextual interpretation is incomplete or ambiguous.
- Fulfills the intended engineering purpose established by SO-F-003.

---

Validation Boundary

Validation of SO-F-003 shall assess whether contextual interpretation fulfills its intended role within the adaptive intelligence architecture.

The correctness of decisions generated from that context and the effectiveness of subsequent actions shall be validated under their respective objectives.

---

Validation Status

Not Yet Validated

---

Validation Notes

Validation evidence should preserve the relationship between representative observations, interpreted operating context, and the downstream functional purpose supported by that context.

Validation shall not require a specific interpretation technology or implementation approach unless such requirements are established by derived engineering artifacts.
